<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="ARTH 113" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2012" href="schedule/2012.xml">2012</calendarYear><term id="120128" href="schedule/2012/fall.xml">Fall 2012</term><subject id="ARTH" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH.xml">Art--History</subject></parents><label>Introduction to African Art</label><description>An introduction to the arts of Africa. Sculpture, textiles, architecture, body adornment, and performance will be examined on the basis of aesthetic, religious, political, and social contexts. The main emphasis will be on traditional art, although the course will address many changes and continuities within African art as evidenced in the late 20th century. The course will proceed geographically from western through central to eastern and southern Africa. Videos, music, and museum visits will complement the lectures.</description><creditHours>4 hours.</creditHours><sectionDegreeAttributes>Non-Western Cultures course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><genEdCategories><category id="CS"><description>Cultural Studies</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1NW">Cultural Studies - Non-West</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCategories><sections><section id="51156" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113/51156.xml">AD1</section><section id="51158" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113/51158.xml">AD3</section><section id="51159" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113/51159.xml">AD4</section><section id="51160" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113/51160.xml">AD5</section><section id="51161" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113/51161.xml">AD6</section><section id="60281" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113/60281.xml">AD7</section><section id="60282" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113/60282.xml">AD8</section><section id="60283" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/113/60283.xml">AD9</section><section id="60284" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTH/11